/-!
# The finitely presented case, first sentence (census key `e19e0d3328ad`)

`simple_kazhdan_sofic_group.tex`, section `sec:questions` (tex l.730–732):

> No group in Theorem~\ref{thm:general}\textup{(b)} is finitely presented:
> a finitely presented LEF group is residually
> finite~\cite{Stepin,VershikGordon}, and an infinite simple group is not.

This is the current text of the sentence.  It was census key `460d289c5b0f` before the section
was reworded, and the corpus endpoint
`Manuscript.SimpleKazhdanSofic.AbstractIntro.manuscriptSentence_generalLimitsNotFinitelyPresented`
states its clauses in the old order.  This module restates them in the printed order.

## Route

* Every group of `thm:general`(b) is `EL_n(R)`, `n ≥ 3`, for `R = LC(C, 𝔽₂) ⋊ Λ` generated by a
  finite `S ∋ 1` and matricial via `φ_k` (`IsMatricialVia`).  By the closed theorem
  `printedSimpleKazhdanGeneral` it is infinite, simple and a marked limit of finite groups, hence
  LEF (`isLEF_of_isMarkedLimit`).  So it is not finitely presented.
* The two reasons are closed corpus theorems: `printedFinitelyPresentedLEFResiduallyFinite`
  (Stepin / Vershik–Gordon, proved over `PresentedGroup` of a finite relator set) and
  `NinetyNineProblems.not_isResiduallyFinite_of_isSimpleGroup_of_infinite`.

No hypothesis beyond those printed in `thm:general`(b) is used.  `IsMatricialVia` also asks
`N_k ≥ 1`, which the printed statement presupposes by speaking of the finite simple groups
`SL_{nN_k}(𝔽₂)`.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation.SimpleKazhdanSofic.SkRows.Questions

open GroupApproximation GroupApproximation.SimpleKazhdanSofic

/-- **tex l.730–732**, in the printed order.
1. No group `EL_n(R)`, `n ≥ 3`, of Theorem `thm:general`(b) is finitely presented.
2. A finitely presented LEF group is residually finite [Stepin, Vershik–Gordon].
3. An infinite simple group is not residually finite. -/
theorem manuscriptSentence_noGeneralGroupFinitelyPresented :
    (∀ (Λ : Type) [Group Λ] [Group.FG Λ] (Z : Type) [TopologicalSpace Z] [CompactSpace Z]
        [TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace Z] [TotallyDisconnectedSpace Z] [PerfectSpace Z]
        [Nonempty Z] [MulAction Λ Z] [ContinuousConstSMul Λ Z], MulAction.IsMinimal Λ Z →
        (∀ ξ : Λ, ξ ≠ 1 → ∀ U : Set Z, IsOpen U → U.Nonempty → ∃ z ∈ U, ξ • z ≠ z) →
        ∀ S : Finset (ClopenGroupCrossedProduct Λ Z (ZMod 2)), 1 ∈ S →
          Subring.closure (S : Set (ClopenGroupCrossedProduct Λ Z (ZMod 2))) = ⊤ →
        ∀ (N : ℕ → ℕ)
          (φ : ∀ k, ClopenGroupCrossedProduct Λ Z (ZMod 2) → Matrix (Fin (N k)) (Fin (N k)) (ZMod 2)),
          IsMatricialVia S N φ → ∀ n : ℕ, 3 ≤ n →
            ¬ Group.IsFinitelyPresented
              ↥(elementaryGroup (Fin n) (ClopenGroupCrossedProduct Λ Z (ZMod 2)))) ∧
      (∀ (E : Type) [Group E], Group.IsFinitelyPresented E → IsLEF E → IsResiduallyFinite E) ∧
      (∀ (E : Type) [Group E] [IsSimpleGroup E] [Infinite E], ¬ IsResiduallyFinite E) := by
  obtain ⟨hfpRF, hsimpleRF, hgeneral⟩ :=
    GroupApproximation.Manuscript.SimpleKazhdanSofic.AbstractIntro.manuscriptSentence_generalLimitsNotFinitelyPresented
  exact ⟨hgeneral, hfpRF, hsimpleRF⟩

#audit_axioms GroupApproximation.SimpleKazhdanSofic.SkRows.Questions.manuscriptSentence_noGeneralGroupFinitelyPresented
#audit_closed_axioms GroupApproximation.SimpleKazhdanSofic.SkRows.Questions.manuscriptSentence_noGeneralGroupFinitelyPresented

end GroupApproximation.SimpleKazhdanSofic.SkRows.Questions
